What command would you use to find files larger than 100MB in Linux?

find /path/to/search -type f -size +100M

How it works:
	•	-type f → Only regular files
	•	-size +100M → Files bigger than 100 MB
	•	+ means “greater than”

To display file sizes in human-readable format:

find . -type f -size +100M -exec ls -lh {} \;

Perfect for cleaning up disk space or troubleshooting storage issues.
